spec:
  grid: 10-18 rows x 10-18 cols, background is black (0)
  bars:
    count: 2 full-span bars on opposite edges (both rows or both columns)
    positions: always row 0 & row H-1, or col 0 & col W-1
    colors: two distinct non-black colors, different from each other
    orientation: either both horizontal (full rows) or both vertical (full cols)
  axis_size: even number (10-18) so no marker can sit at exact midpoint [observed]
  markers:
    color: single non-black color distinct from both bar colors (always 1 [observed])
    count: 6-12 isolated pixels scattered in the interior between bars
    placement: distance >= 2 from nearer bar along bar axis; never at equal distance from both bars
    constraint: the cell one step toward the nearer bar must be background (no collision)
  output:
    for each marker, paint the adjacent cell one step toward the nearer bar with that bar's color
    markers and bars remain unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (constraints are easy to satisfy)
  steps:
    1. Choose orientation (row-bars or col-bars) randomly
    2. Pick grid dimensions H, W in 10-18 (axis along bars must be even)
    3. Choose 3 distinct non-black colors; assign two to bars, one to markers
    4. Fill row 0 / row H-1 (or col 0 / col W-1) with the two bar colors
    5. Place 6-12 marker pixels in the interior (rows 2..H-3 or cols 2..W-3 from bars)
       - ensure each marker's nearer-bar distance != farther-bar distance (guaranteed by even axis)
       - ensure the target cell (one step toward nearer bar) is not occupied by another marker
    6. Verify no two markers paint to the same target cell
```
